ugh he had less than 300 000 views  his posts regularly get over a thousand  likes and of course there's some  variants among these polls but this is  the general picture that you see almost  everywhere personal profiles definitely  get more reach than company profiles on  linkedin so i definitely would encourage  you to use your personal profile as well  and last but not least it seems very  clear to me that the development of  linkedin into an influencer and creator  platform is a key strategic objective of  linkedin they're actively pushing it you  can see it with all the initiatives that  the company is coming up with for  instance the top voices award that now  they award on a yearly basis if you ever  felt like you wanted to build an  influence on instagram on youtube or any  of these other platforms but you were  just too late now is your opportunity  with linkedin because if you start now  you will definitely be still early in  the development of linkedin as a creator  platform the opportunities are out there  you just need to grab them so let's next  talk about the linkedin algorithm and  why should you even care about how the  linkedin algorithm works but then here  again i just looked at some of my own  personal data on my hindi user profile  this is again the data from the first  half year of this year and i just  ordered all the posts by the views that  they received and you can see that  there's quite a significant variance on  the left hand side there are some posts  that got less than 10 000 views again  let me remind you i had about 18 000  followers at that point in time but then  on the right hand side i had a handful  of posts that exceeded 100 000 views and  my most successful post measured in  views received as i just also told you  earlier about  188 000 views and of course views  matters because if people don't see your  content you cannot really spread the  messages that you want to spread you  cannot really work towards the goals and  objectives that you set for yourself in  the beginning and of course if people  don't find your polls they also cannot  find your profile and therefore you also  cannot grow your follower base and your  audience so let's look at how the  linkedin algorithm works behind the  scenes and this is very similar to  almost all the other social media  platform algorithms work this way and i  can imagine this to work is that at the  beginning if you post something linkedin  in the first minutes hours and so on  will show this post to a fraction of  your audience to a fraction of your  followers or to a fraction of the people  who usually enjoy the content that you  create and then they observe what  happens are these people spending time  on the post are they engaging with the  post are they leaving a comment so they  have all these types of indicators that  let the algorithm come to the conclusion  whether this is a good post or not and  so if this post performed well in this  very close group of your most engaged  followers then linkedin will likely show  this post to an extended group of your  followers to almost every one of your  followers and we'll look again how is it  performing is this performing well or  not and again if even with this extended  group linkedin comes to the conclusion  that yes it's a good post then likely it  will show this post to even more people  often also not even your followers  anymore but maybe people who linked them  believes to have similar interests than  the people who follow you people who are  similar to your followers and then again  a regard interest are they interested  are they engaging are they enjoying the  post and then based on that step by step  linkedin will show the post to even more  people up until the point where linkedin  just doesn't find any pockets of people  anymore where the linkedin algorithm  would be confident that these people  would enjoy your post as well and of  course sometimes there are these unicorn  posts where the algorithm comes to the  conclusion that actually more or less  everyone would enjoy it more or less  everyone likes it and then sometimes you  have these super viral posts that are  seen by hundred thousands if not  millions of people it's of course very  difficult to predict to write something  like this but occasionally this might  happen to you so what exactly are these  signals that the algorithm takes into  consideration and what's here important  for me to say is though that i don't  have any inside knowledge behind the  scene knowledge of how the algorithm  works the algorithm is first of all  secret and second it constantly changes  what these are are just some common  assumptions where people test the things  and this is what you will find on many  places on the internet that this is how  it works but it's definitely fair for  yourself to run your own experiment to  see what really benefits your specific  account so let's talk about some  positive signals first one of the most  important things is time on post one of  the key metrics that all these platforms  are optimizing is to keep people keep  users on the platform for as long as  possible because of course the longer  people spend on the platform the more  ads can be shown to these people and  this is usually one of the biggest  monetization levels that the platforms  have so time on post is key but then of  course sharing a post is a positive way  because if you share a post to your  network you're saying that hey this  pause is great it's important it's worth  seeing and worth reading next commenting  so linkedin wants to build a platform  where people engage with each other have  conversations about topics and comments  definitely work towards this goal it's a  key metric of engagement next sending a  post you can send the post to other  users to other people this is a positive  sign of course as well because thereby  you indicate that it's worth sending and  sharing of course if people follow your  profile after they read your post this  speaks towards the post as well and of  course liking a post also liking other  comments will increase engagement in the  same way and then of course they're  negative signals as well so of course  the big negative signals already of  these positive signals don't exist  aren't out there but then surely if  people hide the post so tell the  platform that they don't want to see  content like this this is very negative  if they unfollow you after they read  something from you if they mute the post  from you also if they report the post  that you created these are of course  negative signals from the algorithm and  if so far you received any value from  this video please hit the like button  for the algorithm and also follow or  subscribe to stay up to date on all my  content i will talk more about this  going forward so would love you to stay  on board here next let's talk about some  little tips what you can do to improve  your profile especially with the goal of  becoming a creator and first of all i  would encourage you to use a background  picture many profiles still don't use  background pictures but if someone  visits your profile the first time for  instance after having seen a post in the  feed the background picture is what  really gives your profile character and  you can use it to directly brand  yourself make sure that the key messages  are transported make sure that people  directly understand what you are all  about what they can expect if they  follow you next is the tag line so the  tagline is the line that is displayed  below your name the tagline is very  important because it's shown across many  places on the platform so usually  whenever you write a post below your  name there will also be the tagline  present so this gives the first  impression what is your background what  are you all about why should people be  interested in yourself so make it as  concise and as punchy as possible and  avoid using too many words next are  hashtags so if you turn on the crater  mode i will show you what this is in a  moment you have the opportunity to add  hashtags like this on your profile this  again helps the algorithm to understand  what the niches that you're talking  about what topics you are focusing on  this is also called your authority and  will also help the linkedin search to  place you in the appropriate search  results for this last but not least make  use of the future section so linkedin  provides you with a section where you  can hand select certain posts that you  feel like very well represent what's  going on on your page what you're doing  what you're writing about the signature  pieces of content that you created in  the past make use of that because again  this is the ideal place to give the  first impression to people who are new  to your personal brand or new to your  profile to understand what you're all  about let's now also talk about the  creator mode on your profile you should  find the option to turn on the creator  mode this will give you access to some  additional features that are very  relevant to creators so i would  definitely recommend you to do that for  instance you have access to these  hashtags that i showed you a moment ago  and another thing that automatically  happens if you turn on the creator mode  is that the main call to action on your  profile changes from connect to follow  so usually on standard profiles people  see the connect button so people can  connect with the person but then of  course the other person needs to accept  this connection request this way follow  means that the people want to see your  content want to see your posts but the  other person doesn't need to approve  that so the hurdles are lower people are  not afraid that maybe you won't accept  them so if you change the call to action  to follow this will enable and encourage  more people to follow you and therefore  for you to grow your audience of course  people can still connect with you but  this will not be the main call to action  displayed on your profile anymore let's  now talk about the content strategy and  in this section i want to talk about  some tips some advice some little  tactics and hacks that you can use to  really create the best possible content  for the platform and maximize your  chances to eventually create some  content pieces that will also go viral  and thereby blow up your account what's  important in the very beginning is that  you should think about a niche a topic  that you want to stand for so if people  think about you what do they want to  have in mind what are the key topics  that you want to associate yourself with  so this is called your niche and this  should be rather specific you don't  necessarily from the very first day you  need to have a very tangible first niche  in mind i think it's also fair just to  start with more generic content and then  over time converge towards a niche but  in the medium term you should develop  this for yourself because think about it  if you follow someone why are you  following a profile because you want to  read more of this type of content but if  the content of a person's all over the  place changes all the time  why should someone follow you so think  about your niche first and then from  your niche you can then derive the  content pieces that you want to create  and let's now start by talking about the  anatomy of a successful post on linkedin  and let's start with the hook the post  should always start with a hook so these  are often one or two sentences that just  spark interest create interest let  people want to read more about the post  let's remember the time on post is one  of the most important indicators for the  linkedin algorithm so you want to excite  people you want to motivate people to  read all the posts because this is what  will get you time on post after the hook  there's the body and in this body in the  main part of your 